orange -- blazingly fast XMPP server and client in C++
======================================================

Orange is an XMPP server and a command-line XMPP client for GNU/Linux.
It is in early development: the programs build and answer --help and
--version, but do nothing else yet.

Components
----------

  oranged        the XMPP server                     server/
  orange-agent   per-user daemon holding the client's
                 XMPP sessions, on a unix socket      client/agent/
  orange-cli     subcommands and an interactive mode,
                 talking to orange-agent              client/cli/,
                                                      client/repl/
  liborange      protocol code shared by both         lib/

Requirements
------------

You need a C++23 compiler (GCC 14 or later, or Clang 18 or later with
libstdc++ 14), expat, OpenSSL 3, SQLite 3, standalone asio, libsecret
(for the client) and, for the unit tests, Catch2 3.  On Debian:

    nala install g++ autoconf automake libtool pkgconf texinfo \
      libexpat1-dev libssl-dev libsqlite3-dev libasio-dev catch2 \
      libsecret-1-dev

Building and installing
-----------------------

From a git checkout:

    ./autogen.sh
    ./configure
    make -j"$(nproc)"
    make check

Release tarballs already contain configure, so skip ./autogen.sh there.
See INSTALL for the generic instructions and "info orange" (or
docs/orange.texi) for the Orange-specific configure options.

